  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM &#x2013;  Bangladesh &#x2013; Cyclone Remal - 2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cyclone Remal made landfall in Bangladesh at the end of May 2024, severely affecting southern-western coastal regions. Shortly after the cyclone, floods hit the northeastern region of the country, impacting the population twice in mid-June. The disasters affected an estimated 8.3 million people across 14 districts. In response, the Cyclone and Monsoon Floods Humanitarian Response Plan was launched to support cyclone and flood-affected populations. In alignment with the HRP and the International Organization for Migration Bangladesh Crisis Response Plan 2024, this contribution from Global Affairs Canada aims to support crisis-affected people through shelter assistance, multi-purpose cash assistance, displacement management support and livelihood support as pathways towards durable solutions in Dacope, Khulna, Chhatak and Sunamganj.</narrative>
  </description>
